hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"238","It was narrated by Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli. It was narrated by Al-Fudayl bin Iyadh. Mansour, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman Al-Hajbi, narrated to me. My mother narrated to me. On the authority of Aisha, she said: “I was disputing with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, over the single basin with which we would wash ourselves.”"
"239","Bundar and Muhammad bin Al-Walid told us, they said: Abdul-Ala told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “This place was reserved for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I am in charge of it, so we all proceed in it.”"
"240","We have Bundar, we have Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, we have Ibrahim bin Nafi’ al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Umm Hani, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taking a bath with Maimunah from the same vessel, in a bowl that had traces of dough in it."
